<title>SOUTH KOREA: Seoul creditors extend Jinro affiliates payments.</title>
<headline>Seoul creditors extend Jinro affiliates payments.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-07-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Korean creditor banks on Friday said they decided to extend principal payment to Jinro General Foods Co and Jinro-Coors Brewing Co.</p>
<p>They also said they would supply 8.0 billion won to the struggling Jinro General Foods.</p>
<p>Jinro Industries Co, on the other hand, would be sold to a third party, they said.</p>
<p>The creditors earlier decided to extend principal payment to Jinro Ltd and Jinro Construction Co. They decided to split up and sell Jinro Mass Merchandising.</p>
<p>In April, the 19th-ranked Jinro Group buckled under 3.2 trillion won in debt.</p>
<p>-- Seoul Newsroom (822) 727-5648</p>
</text>
